      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We apply the power rule with $n=3$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4{x}^{3} & = \\\\ {x}^{3}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/id": "e2fcd99b-3b51-589f-9fd0-4c5df6da6a6c",
